# CardioVision AI - Track A Project Checklist & Verification Report

## A. Prediction engine
- [x] Predict overall CAD status.
  - Verification: Implemented in `backend/cardio/service/prediction_service.py` using a calibrated soft-voting ensemble (`CalibratedClassifierCV` wrapping CatBoost, XGBoost, LightGBM, Random Forest, and Extra Trees). Outputs calibrated probability and categorical risk for overall CAD. Verified via backend test suite (`testing/backend/unit/test_prediction_service.py`).
- [x] Predict LAD, LCX and RCA stenosis separately.
  - Verification: Separate `CalibratedClassifierCV` models independently predict stenosis probability for Left Anterior Descending (LAD), Left Circumflex (LCX), and Right Coronary Artery (RCA) vessels (`backend/cardio/service/prediction_service.py`). Verified in unit tests and endpoint tests.
- [x] Use demographic, clinical examination, ECG, laboratory and echocardiographic inputs available in the dataset.
  - Verification: Feature pipeline in `backend/cardio/service/feature_service.py` ingests all categories from the 303-record Z-Alizadeh Sani dataset (demographics like Age/Sex/BMI, vitals like BP/PR, ECG flags like ST elevation/depression/T-inversion/Q-wave/BBB/LVH, laboratory values like lipid profile/FBS/CR/electrolytes/CBC, and echo findings like EF-TTE/RWMA/VHD).
- [x] Prevent target leakage for all four targets.
  - Verification: Target labels (`Cath`, `CAD`, `LAD`, `LCX`, `RCA`) are strictly defined in `LEAKAGE_COLUMNS` (`backend/cardio/constants.py`) and removed from feature matrix `X` before feature engineering and training (`backend/cardio/service/feature_service.py:prepare_training_data`).
- [x] Compare baseline and stronger classifiers using reproducible validation.
  - Verification: Stratified 10-fold cross-validation pipeline in `scripts/train_pipeline.py` compares baseline `LogisticRegression` against `RandomForest`, `ExtraTrees`, `XGBoost`, `LightGBM`, `CatBoost`, and `Soft-Voting Ensemble`. All metrics stored in `artifacts/benchmark_summary.json`.
- [x] Report accuracy, precision, recall, F1-score and ROC-AUC for each target.
  - Verification: `calculate_metrics()` in `scripts/train_pipeline.py` computes accuracy, precision, recall, F1-score, ROC-AUC (as well as specificity and MCC) across all 4 targets and models. Accessible via `/api/v1/benchmarks` and visualized in frontend `BenchmarkModal.tsx`.

