## B. 3D anatomical visualization
- [x] Render a real interactive 3D heart/torso model.
  - Verification: WebGL/Three.js viewer in `frontend/src/components/HeartViewer3D.tsx` renders real anatomical meshes extracted from BodyParts3D FMA 3.2.1 (`BP51939_FMA3_2_1_inference_partof_FMA7088_Heart.zip`, 95,363 vertices and 171,186 triangles across 62 anatomical pieces).
- [x] Identify the LAD, LCX and RCA correctly.
  - Verification: Separate anatomical mesh structures for `lad`, `lcx`, and `rca` are parsed and identified in `frontend/src/utils/anatomy.ts` and `frontend/src/utils/vessels.ts` with correct anatomical descriptions and targeted camera framing (`focusVessel`).
- [x] Color-code each artery using its own prediction probability.
  - Verification: Predictions dynamically map vessel probabilities to color codes (Green <35%, Amber 35%–<65%, Red >=65%) via `vessel_colors_3d` in `backend/cardio/service/prediction_service.py` and rendered as material/emissive colors in `frontend/src/utils/anatomy.ts:updateAnatomyMeshes`.
- [x] Support rotation, zoom and selection of individual vessels.
  - Verification: Three.js `OrbitControls` supports mouse/touch rotation, scroll wheel and +/- button zooming, and individual vessel focus/isolate buttons (`LAD`, `LCX`, `RCA`) with inspection overlays (`frontend/src/components/HeartViewer3D.tsx`).
- [x] Keep the visual state synchronized with the latest inference.
  - Verification: React state synchronizes with `PredictionResponse`. Modifying patient form inputs marks the visual state as stale to prevent misleading interpretations until re-assessed (`frontend/src/pages/DashboardPage.tsx`).

