## C. Clinical dashboard
- [x] Show overall CAD status and all three vessel probabilities.
  - Verification: `frontend/src/components/RiskSummaryCards.tsx` presents CAD, LAD, LCX, and RCA probability percentages, categorical risk bands, and colored risk progress meters.
- [x] Show patient physiological measurements.
  - Verification: `frontend/src/components/PatientForm.tsx` organizes physiological measurements into structured collapsible sections (Profile, History & Risk Factors, Vitals & Physical Exam, Symptoms, ECG, Labs, Echo) allowing display and editing of all patient vitals and biomarkers.
- [x] Explain the current prediction using SHAP or another appropriate interpretation method.
  - Verification: `backend/cardio/service/prediction_service.py` uses TreeSHAP (`shap.TreeExplainer`) on independent surrogate models to compute patient-level attributions. Rendered as interactive contribution charts in `frontend/src/components/SHAPExplanationChart.tsx`.
- [x] Show a visible educational/decision-support disclaimer.
  - Verification: Persistent visible disclaimers are presented in the application footer ("Research MVP · Experimental estimates, not a diagnosis"), under prediction results ("Model probabilities are experimental estimates..."), within the Anatomy and Benchmark guide modals, and returned via API responses (`CLINICAL_SAFETY_DISCLAIMER`).

